-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Interfaces and reference material (no code copied)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Ranix implements the Linux system call ABI and several Linux device uAPIs
(io_uring, DRM, i915, termios, signalfd, statx, ...). Numbers, constants and
structure layouts are transcribed so that unmodified Linux programs run; the
transcriptions are Ranix's own and are checked against the published headers.
Some drivers were written with the help of public datasheets and of other
operating systems' drivers, named in the file headers (for example
drivers/net/rtl8168.c: FreeBSD and OpenBSD re(4), SerenityOS, Realtek
datasheets).

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Removed or replaced before the first EUPL release
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

- kernel/tty/font8x16.h: matched the Linux kernel's GPL-2.0 font_8x16.c. Unused;
  deleted. Spleen (above) is the console font.
- doomgeneric/: GPL-2.0-or-later (one file GPL-3.0-or-later). Not part of the
  kernel; moved out of this tree.
- drivers/net/bcmgenet.c (Raspberry Pi 4 Ethernet): the earlier version's
  header named GPL drivers as its documentation, and a similarity scan found the
  structure of U-Boot's GPL-2.0+ driver in it. Replaced by a clean-room rewrite
  from FreeBSD's BSD-2-Clause driver (item 6 above).
- drivers/net/rtw8723.c (Realtek RTL8723BE Wi-Fi): a side-by-side reading found
  the bring-up sequences and constants of Linux rtlwifi/rtl8723be (GPL-2.0) in
  the earlier version, although its header said otherwise. Replaced by a
  clean-room rewrite from FreeBSD rtwn(4), ISC and BSD-2-Clause (item 5 above).
- arch/aarch64/linker_raspi4.ld and vdso/vdso_layout.lds were rewritten from
  scratch; the old raspi4 script carried lines from the MIT-licensed
  raspi3-tutorial (Copyright bzt). Output is byte-identical.

Older Ranix code published elsewhere (github.com/RasifoX/ranix, and the ranix.org
text that called it "GPLv2") is not covered by this notice.
